gorm calls Close() on a wrapped *sql.DB

gorm.Open allows us to wrap an existing sql.DB connection instead of opening a new one. But sometimes (in case when database is unavailable) gorm closes wrapped connection.

https://github.com/jinzhu/gorm/blob/0fd395ab37aefd2d50854f0556a4311dccc6f45a/main.go#L82
```golang
	// Send a ping to make sure the database connection is alive.
	if d, ok := dbSQL.(*sql.DB); ok {
		if err = d.Ping(); err != nil {
			d.Close()
		}
	}
```
In this case connection becomes unavailable to the external code which is supposed to manage it's lifecycle.

