Bug: Error in emit callback causes the actor to crash

### XState version

XState version 5

### Description
By registering a callback (that throws) to an emit you can cause the actor to stop handling any new events (due to reaching final error state). IMHO the actors should be as independent as possible from its listeners.

### Expected result

The error is thrown in a separate macro task (using _reportUnhandledError_) as with errors thrown by any actor.subscribe-callback. The actor does not go to a final error state but continues unaffected. 


### Actual result

The actor goes to a final error state and stops handling any succeeding events. The test in emit.test.ts seems to indicate that this might be intentional?

