Bug: Cancelled delayed transition on transition in parallel states (v5)

### Description

If a transition into a parallel state is executed, the pending delayed transition in the current state node is cancelled.

```javascript
Waiting: { 
  after: {
    2000: "Fetching"  // a delayed transition
  },
  on: {
    // 🪲 if this transition is triggered, the delayed transition to Fetching never occurs
    // #root.Mode.Demo is a parallel state to #root.Operation.Waiting
    TOGGLE_MODE: {
      target: "#root.Mode.Demo"
    }
  }
}
```

### Expected result

The machine should transition into the #root.Operation.Fetching state after 2000 ms after first entering the Waiting state.

### Actual result

The delayed transition to #root.Operation.Fetching never occurs.

### Reproduction

https://codesandbox.io/s/crazy-dan-jzmhvr?file=/src/index.js

### Additional context

This is an issue with xstate v5.
Occurs with: xstate@5.0.0-beta.34

**Related:** 

https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/issues/4218
https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/pull/4234

The consideration to make:
Should the machine **reenter** the Waiting state when it performs a transition in the parallel state? Reentering Waiting would mean restarting the delayed transition to Fetching.
I feel the Waiting state should not be reentered, since the target of the transition is in a parallel state #root.Mode.

